# Everything in here is generated — nothing the build needs.
# The build itself requires only: Makefile, include/, src/, tests/,
# ASI_SDK/ (the vendored ZWO SDK: libASICamera2.so.1.41 per arch under
# x64/ armv6/ armv7/ armv8/ + the unversioned libASICamera2.so symlinks +
# ASICamera2.h + license.txt) — plus README.md, which `make package` ships
# in package/.

# --- build artifacts (all removed by `make clean`) --------------------------
# generated moc sources, object files, .d dependency files
/build/
# compiled binaries (GUI app + the standalone probes)
/camera_app
/camera_probe
/usb_bench
/wb_probe
# self-contained portable folder assembled by `make package`
/package/

# --- generated camera output -------------------------------------------------
# photo / video / interval-sequence output
/photos/
/videos/
/sequences/
# .ser regression samples (regenerated by ./camera_app --sertest)
/samples/
# --uishot screenshots: `--uishot shot` writes shot + shot.busy.png at the
# root; the documented WB test writes resources/wb_visible.png + .busy.png
/shot
resources/wb_visible.png
*.busy.png

# --- vendored / local, not part of the build ---------------------------------
# If the full ZWO vendor SDK tree is ever re-downloaded (asi-cam.com) into
# ASI_linux_mac_SDK_V1.41/ (e.g. for the not-vendored macOS / 32-bit x86
# libs), it stays out of git — the build needs only the committed ASI_SDK/
# copy (all four Linux archs are vendored there).
/ASI_linux_mac_SDK_V1.41/
# locally downloaded developer tools (GitHub CLI etc.)
/.tools/
